:Salt|Salt]]\n*[[Cookbook:Malt vinegar|Malt vinegar]]\n== Procedure ==\n# Clean and scale fish. Place in a [[Cookbook:Baking Dish|baking dish]] large enough for the fish and vinegar.\n# Mix other ingredients, except vinegar, with salt to taste, and pour over fish.\n# Pour over enough vinegar to cover well.\n# Place in moderate [[Cookbook:Oven|oven]] for 40–50 minutes.\n# Lift fish carefully onto serving dish, and strain liquor over top.\n# Let cool and serve.\n\n==Notes, tips, and variations==\n* ''from'' Boscastle W.I. ''in'' Cornish Recipes, Ancient & Modern, 22nd Edition, The Cornwall Federation of Women's Institutes 1965.\n* ''First collected & published by'' Edith Martin, Tregavethan, Truro, 1929, ''for'' The Cornwall F.of W. I.\n\n[[Category:Cornish recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mackerel]]\n[[Category:Baked recipes]]\n[[Category:Main course recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using clove]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Marinated Mackerel","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"4 or more mackerels","sourceText":"4 or more mackerels","amountText":"4 or more mackerels","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"2 fresh bay leaves, chopped","sourceText":"2 fresh bay leaves, chopped","amountText":"2 fresh bay leaves, chopped","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"6 cloves","sourceText":"6 cloves","amountText":"6 cloves","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1 blade of mace","sourceText":"1 blade of mace","amountText":"1 blade of mace","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"1 sprig of fresh thyme","sourceText":"1 sprig of fresh thyme","amountText":"1 sprig of fresh thyme","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"1 onion, chopped","sourceText":"1 onion, chopped","amountText":"1 onion, chopped","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"10 peppercorns","sourceText":"10 peppercorns","amountText":"10 peppercorns","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"Salt","sourceText":"Salt","amountText":"Salt","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-9","name":"Malt vinegar","sourceText":"Malt vinegar","amountText":"Malt vinegar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null}],"steps":[{"n":1,"text":"Clean and scale fish. Place in a baking dish large enough for the fish and vinegar.","sourceText":"Clean and scale fish. Place in a baking dish large enough for the fish and vinegar.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":2,"text":"Mix other ingredients, except vinegar, with salt to taste, and pour over fish.","sourceText":"Mix other ingredients, except vinegar, with salt to taste, and pour over fish.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":3,"text":"Pour over enough vinegar to cover well.","sourceText":"Pour over enough vinegar to cover well.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":4,"text":"Place in moderate oven for 40–50 minutes.","sourceText":"Place in moderate oven for 40–50 minutes.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":5,"text":"Lift fish carefully onto serving dish, and strain liquor over top.","sourceText":"Lift fish carefully onto serving dish, and strain liquor over top.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":6,"text":"Let cool and serve.","sourceText":"Let cool and serve.","durationMinutes":null}],"nutrition":null,"gaps":["Research extraction only; no culinary/editorial review.","Ingredient quantities, units, alternatives, food identities, aggregate duration, and nutrition remain unknown until individually parsed/reviewed.","Source-level CC BY-SA policy applies generally; page-specific exceptions have not been checked."]}},"parsedRecipe":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"wikibooks:115287","recordId":"wikibooks-115287-r4508879","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceRevision":"4508879","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php